{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XhsE4z7J6VSTsoiamDTVUJ","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"success\\\": true, \\\"data\\\": {\\\"path\\\": \\\"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0513/projects/agent_progress_probe/writing_plan.yaml\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"meta:\\\\n  venue: EMNLP 2026 ARR\\\\n  track: LLM Agents\\\\n  paper_type: \\\\\\\"empirical analysis / Findings\\\\\\\"\\\\n  template: null  # TODO: download latest *ACL / ARR template (acl2023.sty or newer)\\\\n  template_note: \\\\\\\"EMNLP 2026 ARR uses standard *ACL format. Worker Step 2 前需先搜索下载最新模板。\\\\\\\"\\\\n  page_limit: 8\\\\n  appendix: unlimited\\\\n  deadline: 2026-05-25\\\\n  core_claim: >\\\\n    Stagnation signals in LLM agents are fundamentally structural: 30 simple features\\\\n    achieve 0.995 in-domain and 0.967 cross-agent F1, decisively surpassing neural\\\\n    embedding probes (0.906/0.751) and LLM-as-judge (+24.3pp), while three temporal\\\\n    label model implementations all fail to improve over majority vote.\\\\n  created_at: 2026-05-14T19:30:00Z\\\\n  gold_set_status: pending  # 650 windows, 人工标注预计 5/17 完成, Patch 补入\\\\n\\\\npaper_outline:\\\\n  - section: abstract\\\\n    word_budget: 250\\\\n    core_bullets:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Problem: LLM agents exhibit semantic stagnation—executing diverse but collectively unproductive action sequences that evade repetition detectors and overwhelm LLM-based judges\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Approach: systematic empirical study via weak supervision pipeline (3 LFs + MV) on 2 SE agents (SWE-Agent 54K windows, OpenHands 150K windows), comparing structural features, NL embedding probe, and LLM-as-judge\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Finding 1 (primary): stagnation signals are structural—30 features achieve RF 0.995 in-domain, GB 0.967 cross-agent, +24.3pp over LLM-judge, encoder-agnostic (3 encoders all >0.90)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Finding 2: LFs exhibit systematic but agent-specific temporal dynamics—cmd_rep leads by -1.87 steps on SWE-Agent but reverses on OpenHands; removing it improves OH F1 by +21.6pp\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Finding 3: three TLM implementations (TWV/HMM/lag-HMM) all fail vs MV; TWV degrades downstream up to -21.7pp in low-conflict 3-LF regime\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"[GOLD_SET_PLACEHOLDER: gold set validation results pending 5/17]\\\\\\\"\\\\n    dependencies: [experiments, method]\\\\n    tables: []\\\\n    figures: []\\\\n    registry_refs: [non-nlp-baseline, cross-agent-structural, baseline-llm-judge, oh-cmdrep-ablation, temporal-label-model]\\\\n\\\\n  - section: introduction\\\\n    word_budget: 1100\\\\n    core_bullets:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Hook: LLM coding agents fail silently at scale—SlopCodeBench documents 90% verbosity increase and 80% quality erosion in long tasks, yet agents continue reporting confidence. The failure mode is not repetition but semantic stagnation: diverse actions that collectively make no progress\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Gap: existing monitoring detects structural repetition (misses semantic-diverse stagnation), scores individual steps (loses window-level temporal dynamics), or relies on LLM self-evaluation (expensive + limited by the stuck model's own judgment). No systematic study examines WHAT signals actually carry stagnation information\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Insight: stagnation is fundamentally structural—command repetition rates, file diff patterns, and outcome trajectories predict it near-perfectly WITHOUT semantic understanding. This overturns the intuition that detecting subtle agent failures requires sophisticated language understanding\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Contributions: (C1) structural signal discovery—redirects monitoring from representation learning to lightweight features; (C2) LF temporal dynamics—agent-specific roles + circular evaluation methodology; (C3) TLM negative finding—constrains future temporal label model research\\\\\\\"\\\\n    dependencies: [experiments]\\\\n    citation_hints:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"SlopCodeBench (arxiv 2603.24755) for motivation\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"AgentPRM (arxiv 2511.08325) as PRM competitor\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"ICLR 2025 Workshop monitoring paper for sequence-level monitoring\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Snorkel/Ratner for WS background\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"SWE-bench, SWE-Agent, OpenHands for data sources\\\\\\\"\\\\n    figures: [fig_pipeline]\\\\n    tables: []\\\\n    registry_refs: [non-nlp-baseline, cross-agent-structural, baseline-llm-judge, oh-cmdrep-ablation]\\\\n\\\\n  - section: related_work\\\\n    word_budget: 700\\\\n    core_bullets:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Process Reward Models: AgentPRM, InversePRM, ToolPRMBench, trajectory-level RM → need outcome labels + RL pipeline, step-level scoring; we are window-level monitoring via WS, no outcome labels needed\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Agent Self-Reflection & Verification: Reflexion, LATS, ToT, agent verification → intervention not monitoring; relies on the stuck agent itself\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Weak Supervision: Snorkel, FlyingSquid, Safranchik linked HMM (NER-specific) → i.i.d. assumption; our TLM negative finding shows temporal extension does not help in low-conflict LF regimes\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Agent Monitoring & Degradation: SlopCodeBench, ICLR 2025 monitoring, weak-to-strong monitoring → motivates the problem; we provide systematic detection study\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Cycle/Anomaly Detection: CDCS+CDSA, SpecRA, TrajAD → structural repetition only, misses semantic-diverse stagnation\\\\\\\"\\\\n    dependencies: [introduction]\\\\n    citation_hints:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"PRMs: AgentPRM, PRM framework 2502.10325, ToolPRMBench 2601.12294, trajectory RM 2604.08178\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Self-reflection: Reflexion Shinn 2023, LATS Zhou 2023, ToT Yao 2024\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"WS: Snorkel Ratner 2017+2020, FlyingSquid Fu 2020, Safranchik AAAI 2020\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Monitoring: ICLR 2025 Workshop, weak-to-strong 2508.19461\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Degradation: SlopCodeBench 2603.24755\\\\\\\"\\\\n    figures: []\\\\n    tables: []\\\\n    registry_refs: []\\\\n\\\\n  - section: method\\\\n    word_budget: 1300\\\\n    core_bullets:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Problem Formulation: trajectory T = (a_1,...,a_n) → overlapping windows w_i of size k; binary classification y_i ∈ {stagnation, progress}; window-level captures temporal dynamics lost by step-level scoring\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Weak Supervision Pipeline: 3 labeling functions → majority vote → silver labels; confidence = number of agreeing LFs; conf≥2 subset for high-quality evaluation\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"LF Design: (1) command_repetition—ratio of repeated commands in window; (2) file_diff_delta—frequency of code changes; (3) outcome_backpropagation—distant supervision from task outcome propagated backward. Each targets a different stagnation signal\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Structural Feature Extraction: 30 dimensions per window—repetition rates (exact/fuzzy), unique command ratio, file operation counts, edit distances, output entropy, action type distribution. No embedding model required\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"NL Embedding Probe (ProgressProbe): GRU (hidden=256, layers=2) + attention pooling over Qwen3-Embedding-0.6B (1024-dim) window embeddings → binary classification. Baselines: mean-pool + LR, cosine similarity\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"LLM-as-Judge Baseline: Claude Sonnet zero-shot window-level classification\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Temporal Label Models: (a) TWV—Gaussian-weighted smoothing of LF activations with bandwidth σ; (b) HMM—hidden Markov model with LF emissions; (c) Lag-aware HMM—incorporates empirical per-LF temporal offsets\\\\\\\"\\\\n    dependencies: []\\\\n    notation_table:\\\\n      T: \\\\\\\"agent trajectory (a_1, ..., a_n)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      w_i: \\\\\\\"window of k consecutive actions at step i\\\\\\\"\\\\n      k: \\\\\\\"window size (default 5)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      y_i: \\\\\\\"binary label: 0=stagnation, 1=progress\\\\\\\"\\\\n      lambda_j: \\\\\\\"labeling function j ∈ {cmd_rep, file_diff, outcome_bp}\\\\\\\"\\\\n      sigma: \\\\\\\"TWV Gaussian smoothing bandwidth\\\\\\\"\\\\n      conf: \\\\\\\"number of agreeing LFs (1-3)\\\\\\\"\\\\n    figures: [fig_pipeline]\\\\n    tables: [tab_lf_design]\\\\n    registry_refs: [emb_001, probe_001]\\\\n\\\\n  - section: experiments\\\\n    word_budget: 2000\\\\n    core_bullets:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Setup: SWE-Agent (54,809 windows from SWE-bench trajectories, 36% stag) + OpenHands (150,652 windows, 6.6% stag); conf≥2 test set (N=1,824); metric = Macro-F1; circular eval caveat stated upfront\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"§5.1 Main Results (Tab 1): Structural RF 0.9951 > Probe 0.9055 > Mean-pool 0.8435 > LLM-judge 0.6625 > Cosine-sim 0.5606; structural +8.96pp over best neural, +24.3pp over LLM\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"§5.2 Cross-Agent (Tab 1 right cols): Structural GB 0.967 on OH vs Probe 0.528 zero-shot (0.751 with 50% finetune); structural naturally transfers without adaptation\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"§5.3 Robustness: Encoder ablation (SFR/bge-m3/e5-large all >0.90); window size (k=5 optimal, ±5.9pp/1.8pp); data scaling (monotonic 0.805→0.906); multi-seed (mean 0.919±0.011)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"§5.4 LF Temporal Dynamics (Tab 2, Fig 2): cmd_rep leading (-1.87 steps), file_diff concurrent (-1.2), OB lagging (+6.7); all pairwise significant (Bonferroni-corrected); OH reversal: cmd_rep → lagging +3.32 steps\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"§5.5 cmd_rep Ablation (Tab 3): Removing cmd_rep on OH: finetune F1 0.751→0.927 (+21.6pp); root cause: 92.3% firing rate + 71% FP on OH progress windows\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"§5.6 TLM Results (Tab 4): MV 0.895 baseline; TWV σ=2 conf≥2 0.900 (+0.6pp) but downstream degradation -4.9pp in-domain, -21.7pp cross-agent; HMM stag overpredict; lag-HMM 0.894 ≈ MV\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"[GOLD_SET_PLACEHOLDER: §5.7 Gold Set Validation—pending 5/17]\\\\\\\"\\\\n    dependencies: []\\\\n    registry_refs:\\\\n      - non-nlp-baseline      # structural baselines\\\\n      - cross-agent-structural # cross-agent structural\\\\n      - probe_001              # NL probe reference\\\\n      - probe-multiseed        # multi-seed stability\\\\n      - baseline-meanpool-lr   # mean-pool baseline\\\\n      - baseline-llm-judge     # LLM-as-judge\\\\n      - cosinesim-check        # cosine sim baseline\\\\n      - baseline-lf-oracle     # LF oracle\\\\n      - encoder-ablation-probe-bgem3   # encoder ablation\\\\n      - encoder-ablation-probe-e5large # encoder ablation\\\\n      - ablation-window-size   # window size\\\\n      - data-scaling-v2        # data scaling\\\\n      - lf-temporal-dynamics   # LF temporal\\\\n      - oh-cmdrep-ablation     # cmd_rep ablation on OH\\\\n      - oh-full-finetune       # OH full finetune\\\\n      - cross-agent-eval       # probe cross-agent\\\\n      - openhands-fewshot-probe # few-shot transfer\\\\n      - temporal-label-model   # TLM implementations\\\\n      - twv-ablation           # TWV σ sweep\\\\n      - tlm-probe-comparison   # TLM downstream eval\\\\n    tables: [tab_main_results, tab_lf_temporal, tab_oh_cmdrep, tab_tlm_comparison, tab_dataset_stats]\\\\n    figures: [fig_lf_temporal, fig_data_scaling]\\\\n\\\\n  - section: analysis\\\\n    word_budget: 500\\\\n    core_bullets:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Circular Evaluation: structural 0.9951 is expected—features ≈ LF rule inputs, labels = LF rule outputs. This is an upper bound on LF reverse-engineering, not a meaningful detection result. Cross-agent OH (0.967) is non-circular. Gold set is the ultimate arbiter\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Why TLM Fails in 3-LF Regime: conf≥2 agreement rate 95.1% → little room for temporal correction; TWV's conf=1 flips are directionally wrong; need >10 LFs with higher conflict for TLM to potentially help\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Error Analysis: 131 errors (7.2%), 64.9% FP—probe flags windows that LFs miss (semantic-diverse stagnation not covered by 3 LFs)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"OB as Privileged Distant Supervision: 3-seed holdout shows removing OB → -22pp F1; 7.1pp is pure signal contribution beyond cmd_rep+file_diff\\\\\\\"\\\\n    dependencies: [experiments]\\\\n    tables: []\\\\n    figures: []\\\\n    registry_refs: [error-analysis, confidence-gradient, train-without-ob, outcome-bp-3seed]\\\\n\\\\n  - section: conclusion\\\\n    word_budget: 350\\\\n    core_bullets:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Summary: three findings—structural dominance, agent-specific LF dynamics, TLM negative\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Practical implication: agent monitoring should use lightweight structural features (<5ms, no GPU) over expensive embedding or LLM approaches\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Limitations: (1) 2 SE agents—generalization to non-SE agents untested; (2) circular evaluation on LF-derived labels (gold set pending); (3) 3 LFs too few for TLM to show value; (4) no online/intervention evaluation\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Future: non-SE agent domains, online integration, LF scaling, curriculum training from stagnation signals\\\\\\\"\\\\n    dependencies: [experiments, analysis]\\\\n    tables: []\\\\n    figures: []\\\\n    registry_refs: []\\\\n\\\\nvisualization_plan:\\\\n  - fig_id: fig_pipeline\\\\n    type: conceptual\\\\n    tool: paperbanana\\\\n    description: >\\\\n      System pipeline overview: (left) raw agent trajectory → sliding window extraction (k=5);\\\\n      (center) 3 LFs (cmd_rep, file_diff, outcome_bp) → majority vote → silver labels with confidence;\\\\n      (right) three detection approaches compared: structural features (30-dim), NL embedding probe (GRU),\\\\n      LLM-as-judge. Arrows show data flow. Color-code the three approaches.\\\\n    placement: method\\\\n    aspect_ratio: \\\\\\\"2:1\\\\\\\"\\\\n    data_source: \\\\\\\"manual\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  - fig_id: fig_lf_temporal\\\\n    type: statistical\\\\n    tool: matplotlib\\\\n    description: >\\\\n      LF temporal dynamics on SWE-Agent: violin or box plot showing lag distribution\\\\n      (steps relative to stagnation onset) for each LF. X-axis: LF name (cmd_rep, file_diff, outcome_bp).\\\\n      Y-axis: lag (negative=leading, positive=lagging). Horizontal line at 0.\\\\n      Show median, quartiles. Annotate mean lag values. Optional: small inset or side panel\\\\n      showing OH cmd_rep reversal.\\\\n    placement: experiments\\\\n    aspect_ratio: \\\\\\\"4:3\\\\\\\"\\\\n    data_source: \\\\\\\"registry: lf-temporal-dynamics\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  - fig_id: fig_data_scaling\\\\n    type: statistical\\\\n    tool: matplotlib\\\\n    description: >\\\\n      Data scaling curve: X-axis = training data percentage (10%, 25%, 50%, 100%),\\\\n      Y-axis = Macro-F1. Line plot with markers for NL probe performance.\\\\n      Horizontal dashed line for structural RF baseline (0.9951) as reference ceiling.\\\\n      Annotate each point with F1 value. Show the monotonic trend clearly.\\\\n    placement: experiments\\\\n    aspect_ratio: \\\\\\\"3:2\\\\\\\"\\\\n    data_source: \\\\\\\"registry: data-scaling-v2, non-nlp-baseline\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\ntable_plan:\\\\n  - table_id: tab_main_results\\\\n    caption: \\\\\\\"Stagnation detection: structural features vs. neural and LLM approaches. Macro-F1 on conf≥2 test sets. SWE = in-domain SWE-Agent; OH = cross-agent OpenHands transfer.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    placement: experiments\\\\n    type: comparison\\\\n    columns: [Method, \\\\\\\"SWE Macro-F1\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"SWE F1_stag\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"SWE F1_prog\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"OH Macro-F1\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"OH F1_stag\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"OH F1_prog\\\\\\\"]\\\\n    data_source: \\\\\\\"registry: non-nlp-baseline, cross-agent-structural, probe_001, baseline-meanpool-lr, cosinesim-check, baseline-llm-judge, baseline-lf-oracle, cross-agent-eval, oh-full-finetune\\\\\\\"\\\\n    notes: \\\\\\\"Bold best, underline second. Footnote: SWE results are circular (eval on LF-derived labels); OH cross-agent is non-circular. [GOLD_SET] row to be added.\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  - table_id: tab_lf_design\\\\n    caption: \\\\\\\"Labeling function design and per-agent coverage statistics.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    placement: method\\\\n    type: statistics\\\\n    columns: [LF, \\\\\\\"Signal Type\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"SWE Fire Rate\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"SWE Stag Precision\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"OH Fire Rate\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"OH Stag Precision\\\\\\\"]\\\\n    data_source: \\\\\\\"registry: cross-agent-eval, emb_001\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  - table_id: tab_lf_temporal\\\\n    caption: \\\\\\\"Temporal roles of labeling functions relative to stagnation onset (SWE-Agent). All pairwise comparisons significant after Bonferroni correction.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    placement: experiments\\\\n    type: statistics\\\\n    columns: [\\\\\\\"Labeling Function\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Mean Lag (steps)\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"% Leading\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"% Concurrent\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"% Lagging\\\\\\\"]\\\\n    data_source: \\\\\\\"registry: lf-temporal-dynamics\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  - table_id: tab_oh_cmdrep\\\\n    caption: \\\\\\\"Impact of removing command_repetition LF on OpenHands cross-agent transfer. cmd_rep has 92.3% firing rate and 71% false positive rate on OH progress windows.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    placement: experiments\\\\n    type: ablation\\\\n    columns: [LF Config, \\\\\\\"Zero-Shot F1\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Finetune F1\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Finetune F1_stag\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Finetune F1_prog\\\\\\\"]\\\\n    data_source: \\\\\\\"registry: oh-cmdrep-ablation, cross-agent-eval, oh-full-finetune\\\\\\\"\\\\n    baseline_row: \\\\\\\"3-LF (with cmd_rep)\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  - table_id: tab_tlm_comparison\\\\n    caption: \\\\\\\"Temporal label model comparison. None improves over majority vote; TWV degrades downstream classifiers.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    placement: experiments\\\\n    type: comparison\\\\n    columns: [Label Method, \\\\\\\"Conf≥2 F1\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"MV Agreement\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Downstream SWE F1\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Downstream OH F1\\\\\\\"]\\\\n    data_source: \\\\\\\"registry: temporal-label-model, twv-ablation, tlm-probe-comparison\\\\\\\"\\\\n    notes: \\\\\\\"Downstream = probe trained on method's labels, evaluated against MV conf≥2 ground truth.\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  - table_id: tab_dataset_stats\\\\n    caption: \\\\\\\"Dataset statistics.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    placement: experiments\\\\n    type: statistics\\\\n    columns: [Agent, Source, Windows, \\\\\\\"Stag %\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Conf≥2\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Conf≥2 Stag %\\\\\\\"]\\\\n    data_source: \\\\\\\"registry: emb_001, cross-agent-eval\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  # --- Appendix tables ---\\\\n  - table_id: tab_encoder_ablation\\\\n    caption: \\\\\\\"Encoder ablation: NL probe performance is consistent across three embedding models (all >0.90 Macro-F1).\\\\\\\"\\\\n    placement: appendix\\\\n    type: ablation\\\\n    columns: [Encoder, Dim, \\\\\\\"Macro-F1\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"F1_stag\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"F1_prog\\\\\\\"]\\\\n    data_source: \\\\\\\"registry: probe_001, encoder-ablation-probe-bgem3, encoder-ablation-probe-e5large\\\\\\\"\\\\n    baseline_row: \\\\\\\"SFR-Embedding (Qwen3-0.6B)\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  - table_id: tab_window_ablation\\\\n    caption: \\\\\\\"Window size ablation. k=5 is optimal; k=3 loses context, k=7 introduces noise.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    placement: appendix\\\\n    type: ablation\\\\n    columns: [k, \\\\\\\"Macro-F1\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"F1_stag\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"F1_prog\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Δ vs k=5\\\\\\\"]\\\\n    data_source: \\\\\\\"registry: ablation-window-size\\\\\\\"\\\\n    baseline_row: \\\\\\\"k=5\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  - table_id: tab_architecture_ablation\\\\n    caption: \\\\\\\"Probe architecture ablation.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    placement: appendix\\\\n    type: ablation\\\\n    columns: [Architecture, Params, \\\\\\\"Macro-F1\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"F1_stag\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"F1_prog\\\\\\\"]\\\\n    data_source: \\\\\\\"registry: ablation-architecture\\\\\\\"\\\\n    baseline_row: \\\\\\\"GRU + Attention\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  - table_id: tab_multiseed\\\\n    caption: \\\\\\\"Multi-seed stability of the NL embedding probe (5 seeds).\\\\\\\"\\\\n    placement: appendix\\\\n    type: statistics\\\\n    columns: [Seed, \\\\\\\"Macro-F1\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"F1_stag\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"F1_prog\\\\\\\"]\\\\n    data_source: \\\\\\\"registry: probe-multiseed\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\nliterature_strategy:\\\\n  citation_budget: 35\\\\n  macro_context:\\\\n    - \\\\\\\"LLM agent progress monitoring and evaluation\\\\\\\"\\\\n    - \\\\\\\"weak supervision and data programming on sequential data\\\\\\\"\\\\n    - \\\\\\\"process reward models for LLM agents\\\\\\\"\\\\n  micro_clusters:\\\\n    - cluster_name: \\\\\\\"process-reward-models\\\\\\\"\\\\n      search_queries:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"process reward model LLM agent 2025 2026\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"AgentPRM step-level evaluation agent trajectory\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"trajectory reward model agent planning verification\\\\\\\"\\\\n      must_cite:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"AgentPRM (Xi et al., 2511.08325)\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"PRM Framework (Choudhury, 2502.10325)\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"ToolPRMBench (Li et al., 2601.12294)\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"Trajectory-level RM (2604.08178)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      target_count: 6\\\\n\\\\n    - cluster_name: \\\\\\\"agent-self-reflection\\\\\\\"\\\\n      search_queries:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"LLM agent self-reflection self-correction 2024 2025\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"Reflexion LATS tree of thoughts agent verification\\\\\\\"\\\\n      must_cite:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"Reflexion (Shinn et al., NeurIPS 2023)\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"LATS (Zhou et al., 2023)\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"Tree of Thoughts (Yao et al., NeurIPS 2024)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      target_count: 5\\\\n\\\\n    - cluster_name: \\\\\\\"weak-supervision\\\\\\\"\\\\n      search_queries:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"data programming weak supervision sequential temporal 2024 2025\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"Snorkel label model programmatic labeling\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"weak supervision for NLP annotation\\\\\\\"\\\\n      must_cite:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"Snorkel (Ratner et al., VLDB 2017 / NeurIPS 2020)\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"FlyingSquid (Fu et al., ICML 2020)\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"Linked HMM for sequence tagging (Safranchik et al., AAAI 2020)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      target_count: 5\\\\n\\\\n    - cluster_name: \\\\\\\"agent-monitoring-degradation\\\\\\\"\\\\n      search_queries:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"LLM agent monitoring degradation evaluation 2025 2026\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"coding agent quality degradation long context\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"SlopCodeBench agent stagnation loop\\\\\\\"\\\\n      must_cite:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"SlopCodeBench (2603.24755, 2026)\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"Monitoring LLM Agents for Sequentially Contextual Harm (ICLR 2025 Workshop)\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"Reliable Weak-to-Strong Monitoring (2508.19461)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      target_count: 6\\\\n\\\\n    - cluster_name: \\\\\\\"agent-benchmarks\\\\\\\"\\\\n      search_queries:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"SWE-bench coding agent benchmark 2024\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"OpenHands CodeAct agent platform\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"coding agent evaluation framework\\\\\\\"\\\\n      must_cite:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"SWE-bench (Jimenez et al., ICLR 2024)\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"SWE-Agent (Yang et al., 2024)\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"OpenHands (Wang et al., 2024)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      target_count: 5\\\\n\\\\n    - cluster_name: \\\\\\\"cycle-anomaly-detection\\\\\\\"\\\\n      search_queries:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"agent action cycle detection repetition 2024 2025\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"trajectory anomaly detection sequential\\\\\\\"\\\\n      must_cite: []\\\\n      target_count: 4\\\\n\\\\n    - cluster_name: \\\\\\\"embedding-representation\\\\\\\"\\\\n      search_queries:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"text embedding model comparison SFR e5 bge 2024 2025\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"sentence embedding for classification\\\\\\\"\\\\n      must_cite: []\\\\n      target_count: 4\\\\n\\\\nwriting_order:\\\\n  - experiments   # 先写：最多数据，锚定全文数字\\\\n  - method        # 次写：依赖 experiments 确定的 notation 和 scope\\\\n  - analysis      # 依赖 experiments 章节的具体结果\\\\n  - introduction  # 依赖 experiments + analysis 确定 story spine\\\\n  - related_work  # 依赖 introduction 的 positioning\\\\n  - abstract      # 全文摘要\\\\n  - conclusion    # 最后，总结 + limitations\\\", \\\"total_chars\\\": 20385, \\\"truncated\\\": false}, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"metadata\\\": {}}\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01B8qV6UnA5DW1MGFvUGp9VP","session_id":"e100e194-7f3c-443d-b4ce-e36ca0f83e44","uuid":"e1c9c3ac-0572-4229-9f24-848661fd827d","timestamp":"2026-05-14T19:12:55.787Z"}
